# Environment files
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Package manager. `bun.lock` IS committed — deliberately breaking the repo-root convention that
# excludes lockfiles, because this project is the one that gets deployed.
#
# Without it, Vercel resolves ~30 direct dependencies and a much larger transitive tree — web3.js,
# Anchor, the MagicBlock SDK, pixi — fresh on every build. A broken patch release anywhere in that
# tree then produces a deploy that differs from the build that was tested, with nothing in the diff
# to show it. A lockfile is how "it worked when I checked" stays true on a machine we don't control.
#
# The other lockfiles stay ignored: two package managers' locks in one directory is a race about
# which one is authoritative.
bun.lockb
package-lock.json
pnpm-lock.yaml

